Hello fellow hackers,

I`m working in a networked environment and just right now I (we) have
a small problem:

All the lockfiles are kept in the same directory. This allows at most
26 hack players on our campus. This number is a bit small but usually
sufficient.

The real problem is that a lockfile is not removed when a player's
machine crashes, so old (and useless) lockfiles block the game.

Solution 1: Contact your system manager ("Hey, I want to play hack
during work, would you please delete bogus lock files?")

Solution 2: Place lockfiles in /tmp. /tmp is automagically cleared
each time the system is booted -> no bogus lockfiles.

What do you think?
Ulrich
